{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"fb303eab-d9b3-4aab-ae9c-6dac275a1511","status":"SUCCESS","response":"The normalization audit of the backend schema ([`supabase/migrations/`](file:///tmp/h-PUoSN1/supabase/migrations)) and server functions ([`supabase/functions/`](file:///tmp/h-PUoSN1/supabase/functions)) has been written to [**`ANSWER.md`**](file:///tmp/h-PUoSN1/ANSWER.md).\n\n### Summary of Findings\n\nFollowing Kent's 1983 formulation (*\"a fact about the key, the whole key, and nothing but the key\"*) and the three-step audit criteria from the guide:\n\n1. **Second Normal Form (2NF — \"the whole key\"):**\n   - **[`idea_items.person_id`](file:///tmp/h-PUoSN1/supabase/migrations/20261008230200_backend_v1.sql#L93):** Primary key is `(idea_id, item_id)`, but `person_id` functionally depends on `item_id` alone (`items.person_id`). Dropped in [`20261010040000_normal_forms.sql`](file:///tmp/h-PUoSN1/supabase/migrations/20261010040000_normal_forms.sql#L73-L123) and resolved via joins in queries and recount triggers.\n\n2. **Third Normal Form (3NF — \"nothing but the key\"):**\n   - **[`document_chunks`](file:///tmp/h-PUoSN1/supabase/migrations/20261008230100_knowledge_chunks.sql#L35-L49) parent columns:** `kind`, `label`, `source_url`, and `source_ref` were duplicated from parent [`documents`](file:///tmp/h-PUoSN1/supabase/migrations/20261008170000_init.sql#L225). Dropped in migration `20261010040000` and joined through `match_document_chunks`.\n   - **[`documents.is_public`](file:///tmp/h-PUoSN1/supabase/migrations/20261008230100_knowledge_chunks.sql#L26):** Functionally determined by `label` (`is_public = (label = 'quotable')`). Replaced with a stored generated column.\n   - **[`drafts.tokens_in` and `drafts.tokens_out`](file:///tmp/h-PUoSN1/supabase/migrations/20261008170000_init.sql#L179-L180):** Deterministic functions of the `tokens` breakdown JSON (`input + cache_read + cache_write` and `output`). Replaced with stored generated columns using `hb_json_int`.\n   - **[`people.first_touch_at` and `people.last_touch_at`](file:///tmp/h-PUoSN1/supabase/migrations/20261008170000_init.sql#L118-L119):** Aggregate extrema (`min`/`max`) over [`touches`](file:///tmp/h-PUoSN1/supabase/migrations/20261008170000_init.sql#L195) previously written by app code. Assigned exclusively to trigger `touches_person_span`.\n   - **`project_id` across child tables:** Redundancy retained for RLS performance, but protected against drift using composite foreign keys (`(parent_id, project_id) references parent(id, project_id)`).\n\n3. **Current / Reintroduced 3NF Violations (in [`20261015010000_ask_code_model_calls.sql`](file:///tmp/h-PUoSN1/supabase/migrations/20261015010000_ask_code_model_calls.sql)):**\n   - **[`model_calls`](file:///tmp/h-PUoSN1/supabase/migrations/20261015010000_ask_code_model_calls.sql#L15-L33) (`tokens_in`, `tokens_out`, `cost_usd`):** Plain columns written manually in server code alongside `usage` JSONB rather than using stored generated columns.\n   - **[`model_calls.project_id`](file:///tmp/h-PUoSN1/supabase/migrations/20261015010000_ask_code_model_calls.sql#L20) \u0026 [`code_questions.project_id`](file:///tmp/h-PUoSN1/supabase/migrations/20261015010000_ask_code_model_calls.sql#L58):** Both tables store `project_id` alongside `item_id references items(id)` without a composite foreign key `(item_id, project_id) references items(id, project_id)`, allowing the copies to disagree.\n   - **[`code_questions.cost_usd`](file:///tmp/h-PUoSN1/supabase/migrations/20261015010000_ask_code_model_calls.sql#L74):** Hand-written derived value duplicate of `usage-\u003e\u003e'cost_usd'`, manually aggregated across `model_calls` on failure by application code.\n\n4. **First Normal Form (1NF — non-atomic collections):**\n   - **[`plans.allowed_models`](file:///tmp/h-PUoSN1/supabase/migrations/20261009200000_plans_user_model.sql#L19):** Stored as a `text[]` array and queried with `= any`. Normalized into table [`plan_models`](file:///tmp/h-PUoSN1/supabase/migrations/20261010040000_normal_forms.sql#L278-L284).\n\nFull details, schemas, functional dependencies, and remediation SQL are documented in [**`ANSWER.md`**](file:///tmp/h-PUoSN1/ANSWER.md).\n","duration_seconds":513.818515,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":233782,"output_tokens":55530,"thinking_tokens":44395,"cache_read_tokens":3321718,"total_tokens":289312}}}
